  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "From a point on the ground, the angle of elevation to the top of a building is measured as \\(45^\\circ\\). The horizontal distance from this point to the base of the building is \\(40\\text{ m}\\). Ignoring eye height, find the height of the building. (Unit: m)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "40",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\tan 45^\\circ=1\\), so the building height is \\(40\\times\\tan 45^\\circ=40\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Equal angles give equal sides\n\nThe building, the horizontal ground segment, and the line of sight form a right triangle. Its other acute angle is \\(90^\\circ-45^\\circ=45^\\circ\\), so the two acute angles are equal. Their opposite sides are therefore equal, giving a building height of \\(40\\text{ m}\\).",
